Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 05:16:51 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 130/161] hjviewer: the chat windows in the app's look (U15)

U15 (UX-S5), the desktop part, second commit. chat_page.dart serves
the session window's chat, the PC's connection window (CM) and
Android's main chat page; all three change together (U15-D8).

- Bubbles through hjvChatBubbleColors: one's own on primaryFill with
  white text and time, the other side's on fill in the text colour
  with a textSecondary time; MessageOptions gets the same colours for
  the default builders. Text 14/1.4, time 12 px with digits of one
  width (was 8 px white), the large radius with a 4 px tail.
- The input field takes the theme's look (fill, no border, the focus
  ring); the send icon and Android's chat list arrows in primary, the
  online dot in success.
- overlay.dart: the floating chat window (desktop, Android and iOS's
  IOSDraggable) keeps a clear frame over the remote screen: a
  borderStrong border and the card's shadow (review R3, instead of the
  lighter border). The phone's chat head (was a blue bar with white
  20 px WorkSans) is drawn in place in _buildMobileAppBar (review R5,
  no unused upstream copy): the canvas grey with a bottom border, so
  the head to drag stands off the chat, 'Chat' 17/700, the icons 24 px
  textSecondary. The desktop head stays as it was.

No text changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
